<title>USA: Churchill Downs amends special meeting rule.</title>
<headline>Churchill Downs amends special meeting rule.</headline>
<dateline>LOUISVILLE, Ky. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Churchill Downs Inc said Thursday that its stockholders have approved an amendment to its articles of incorporation to increase the percentage of shares needed to call a special meeting.</p>
<p>Under the amended rules, 66-2/3 percent is required rather than the prior 33-1/3 percent, the company said.</p>
<p>The annual meeting was held Thursday.</p>
<p>Churchill Downs owns the racetrack of the same name, where the Kentucky Derby is held annually.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
